  "test_plan_vector": null,
  "spec": [
    "Platform Verification 4: MUST evaluate `seq` and `prev` continuity per `(iss, mandate_ref)` chain. A byte-identical redelivery of a receipt the platform already holds is ignored. A second, different receipt for a `seq` the platform already holds is `receipt_sequence_gap`; the platform keeps both."
  ],
  "signing": "TEST-ONLY P-256 keys derived from fixed labels in common/payments/ap2_receipt_fixtures.py; deterministic ECDSA (RFC 6979). Never use them outside these vectors.",
  "notes": "Receipts 1 and 2 are both seq 2, with different processing entries. The one held first stays in the chain, so receipt 3 (seq 3, whose prev is receipt 1) continues it. The second is reported as a gap and neither chained nor counted; the platform keeps both. Recomputation stops at that gap, so receipt 3 is not compared with recomputed totals; its stated totals are within the mandate. A byte-identical redelivery of a held receipt would be ignored, not a gap.",
